[Chapter "Early queen moves"]
[Line "Queen guards c4: 4.Qc2"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Accepted: Mannheim Variation"]

{White protects c4 with the queen. Black takes anyway and develops.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit: White attacks d5.} 2... c6 {The Slav: support d5 with a pawn and keep the c8 bishop's diagonal open, unlike ...e6.} 3. Nf3 Nf6 {Develop and guard d5 again.} 4. Qc2 {White protects c4 with the queen.} 4... dxc4 {Take anyway: the queen has to spend another move taking back.} 5. Qxc4 Bf5 {Bishop out before ...e6.} 6. Nc3 e6 {Close the chain behind the bishop.} 7. g3 Nbd7 {Develop; ...Be7 and castling come next.} *
